skythlikesclouds Could you test the fix on this MRP?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5025653681/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5317712061","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117833#issuecomment-5317712061","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117833","id":5317712061,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPPXYvQ","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-17T16:30:31Z","updated_at":"2026-08-17T16:30:31Z","body":"As I guessed it looks wrong. I'd guess it's because the environment BRDF is inherently different between Forward+ and Mobile since the former was updated to use multiscattering.\n\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a49aeff-9ca9-481d-8061-e729d1ed0c4f\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5317712061/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5317868070","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117833#issuecomment-5317868070","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117833","id":5317868070,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPPg6Jg","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-17T16:48:27Z","updated_at":"2026-08-17T16:49:54Z","body":"In practice basically everyone uses the single scattering approximation on mobile since it avoids doing a texture fetch (which means it is significantly faster and leaves more bandwidth for other things.) See https://www.unrealengine.com/en-US/blog/physically-based-shading-on-mobile\n\nTo get the energy compensating term, you need to use an LUT. Which is fine if you already use an LUT for the DFG term. But for mobile it means adding an extra LUT that you didn't have before, which really sucks. \n\nIMO there is nothing actionable here. The point of having 3 renderers is that we can make different tradeoffs to target different classes of devices. If we try to force the mobile and compatibility renderer to look and behave the same as the forward+ renderer then there won't be any point in having them. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5317868070/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]